From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ahmedawachi <121810925+ahmedawachi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 09:29:28 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] cygwin: expose dladdr()/Dl_info in debug.c without
 editing system headers

What: on __CYGWIN__ builds (Cygwin and MSYS2), debug.c now sets
__GNU_VISIBLE to 1 only around its own #include <dlfcn.h>, then restores
it to 0. Every other platform, and a Cygwin build that already defines
_GNU_SOURCE, takes the unchanged plain #include.

Why: Cygwin's <dlfcn.h> declares Dl_info and
dladdr() only under "#if __GNU_VISIBLE", newlib sets that only for
_GNU_SOURCE, and fmacros.h defines _GNU_SOURCE only on Linux, so debug.c
(dumpX86Calls, dumpCodeAroundEIP) does not compile on either toolchain.
The redis-windows CI worked around it with
"sed -i 's/__GNU_VISIBLE/1/' /usr/include/dlfcn.h", which mutates the
toolchain and was persisted by the cached C:/cygwin64. This patch has the
same effect as that sed, limited to debug.c, so the produced code is
unchanged. It deliberately does not define _GNU_SOURCE for the file:
that would also switch strerror_r() and basename() to their GNU variants
and widen every other header's visibility.

Risk: very low. Preprocessor-only change inside one file; no code path
changes on any platform. If a future runtime pulls <dlfcn.h> in earlier
(through another header) the declarations stay hidden and the build fails
loudly, exactly as it does today without the sed.
---
 src/debug.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/debug.c b/src/debug.c
index 24c8c7d..475ae08 100644
--- a/src/debug.c
+++ b/src/debug.c
@@ -27,7 +27,20 @@
 
 #include <arpa/inet.h>
 #include <signal.h>
+#if defined(__CYGWIN__) && !__GNU_VISIBLE
+/* Cygwin/MSYS2 <dlfcn.h> declares Dl_info and dladdr() only when
+ * __GNU_VISIBLE is set, and fmacros.h defines _GNU_SOURCE only on Linux.
+ * Expose just those declarations rather than compiling this file in GNU
+ * mode, which would also switch strerror_r() and basename() to their GNU
+ * variants. */
+#undef __GNU_VISIBLE
+#define __GNU_VISIBLE 1
 #include <dlfcn.h>
+#undef __GNU_VISIBLE
+#define __GNU_VISIBLE 0
+#else
+#include <dlfcn.h>
+#endif
 #include <fcntl.h>
 #include <sys/mman.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
